IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpfta-types`

-- Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, Part 3A (ss 19 to 26):
-- investigation powers.  Source: source/CPFTA2003.txt lines 1303 to 1843.
--
-- These are powers of the Commission and duties on its officers.  Each power is
-- encoded as whether it is available on the facts, each duty as whether it has been
-- met.  Powers that only enumerate what an entrant may do once lawfully on premises
-- (ss 21(5), 22(3)) give no condition of their own beyond entry and are encoded as
-- that availability.

§ `Part 3A -- Investigation powers`

§§ `19. Power to investigate`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 19(1)(a) and (b)"
GIVEN s IS A `Suspicion Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Commission may conduct an investigation` IF
        s's `there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that a supplier has engaged, is engaging or is likely to engage in an unfair practice`
     OR s's `there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that a person has knowingly abetted, aided, permitted or procured a supplier to engage in an unfair practice`
     OR s's `there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that a person is knowingly abetting, aiding, permitting or procuring a supplier to engage in an unfair practice`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 19(2)(a) and (b)"
GIVEN o IS AN `Officer Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is validly appointed an investigation officer` IF
        o's `the chief executive made the appointment`
    AND (CONSIDER o's `kind of appointee`
         WHEN `an officer or employee of the Commission` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `an auxiliary police officer appointed under Part 9 of the Police Force Act 2004` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `any other person` THEN FALSE)

-- 19(3)(a) applies only to an officer or employee of the Commission; 19(3)(b) applies
-- "on demand", so the field records that the card was produced whenever it was
-- demanded (TRUE where it was never demanded).

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 19(3)(a) and (b)"
GIVEN o IS AN `Officer Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer has complied with section 19(3)` IF
        (CONSIDER o's `kind of appointee`
         WHEN `an officer or employee of the Commission` THEN o's `the officer declared the officer's office`
         OTHERWISE TRUE)
    AND o's `the officer, on demand, produced to the person affected the identification card the chief executive issued`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 19(4)"
GIVEN o IS AN `Officer Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the refusal to comply is not an offence because the officer did not comply with section 19(3)` IF
        o's `the person refuses to comply with a request, demand or order of the officer`
    AND NOT `the officer has complied with section 19(3)` o

§§ `20. Power to require documents, articles or information`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 20(2)(a) and (b)"
GIVEN n IS A `Document Notice Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice complies with section 20(2)` IF
        n's `the notice indicates the purpose for which the document, article or information is required`
    AND n's `the notice is accompanied by a copy of the offences under sections 27, 28, 29 and 30`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 20(1) and (2)"
GIVEN n IS A `Document Notice Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Commission may require the production of a document or article or the provision of information` IF
        n's `the notice is in writing`
    AND n's `the notice is given to a supplier or person mentioned in section 19(1)`
    AND n's `the Commission considers the specified document, article or information relevant to the investigation`
    AND `the notice complies with section 20(2)` n

-- 20(3) (the Commission may specify time, place, manner and form), 20(4) (the power
-- includes copies, explanations and statements of where a document is) and 20(5)
-- (what "specified" means) extend the power and add no condition: inert.

§§ `21. Power to enter premises without warrant`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 21(2)(a), (b) and (c)"
GIVEN e IS AN `Entry Without Warrant Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice requirements of section 21(2) are met` IF
        e's `the occupier was given a written notice`
    AND e's `the number of working days' notice of the intended entry given in the notice` AT LEAST 2
    AND e's `the notice indicates the subject matter and purpose of the investigation`
    AND e's `the notice is accompanied by a copy of the offences under sections 27, 28, 29 and 30`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 21(3) and (4)(a) and (b)"
GIVEN e IS AN `Entry Without Warrant Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the alternative requirements of section 21(3) and (4) are met` IF
        e's `the investigation officer has taken all the steps that are reasonably practicable to give notice but has not been able to do so`
    AND e's `evidence of the authorisation of the investigation officer and of every authorised assistant is produced`
    AND e's `a document containing the information about subject matter, purpose and the offences is produced`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 21(1) to (5)"
GIVEN e IS AN `Entry Without Warrant Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the entry without warrant is permitted, with the powers of section 21(5)` IF
        e's `the entry is in connection with an investigation under section 19(1)`
    AND e's `the premises are reasonably suspected of being used by the person under investigation in connection with an unfair practice`
    AND e's `the entrant is an investigation officer, or a person the Commission has authorised in writing to accompany and assist`
    AND (   `the notice requirements of section 21(2) are met` e
         OR `the alternative requirements of section 21(3) and (4) are met` e)

§§ `22. Power to enter premises under warrant`

-- 22(2)(a) to (d): the conditions.  22(4): a warrant issued on ground (b) or (c) may
-- also authorise the power in respect of any other document relating to the
-- investigation that it is reasonable to suspect is on the premises.

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 22(1) and (2)(a) to (d)"
GIVEN w IS A `Warrant Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may issue a warrant` IF
        w's `the applicant is the Commission`
    AND w's `the warrant names an investigation officer and one or more authorised assistants`
    AND NOT null (w's `the conditions established for the premises`)

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 22(4)"
GIVEN w IS A `Warrant Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may authorise the power in respect of any other document` IF
        `the court may issue a warrant` w
    AND any (GIVEN c YIELD
                 CONSIDER c
                 WHEN `there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that there are on any premises documents which the Commission may require under section 20, and that if required they would be concealed, removed, tampered with or destroyed` THEN TRUE
                 WHEN `there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that there are on any premises documents or goods within section 21, and that if notice is given under section 21(2) they would be concealed, removed, tampered with or destroyed` THEN TRUE
                 OTHERWISE FALSE)
            (w's `the conditions established for the premises`)

-- 22(6): the warrant continues in force for one month beginning on the day it is
-- issued; it must indicate subject matter and purpose and be accompanied by a copy of
-- the offences.  "One month beginning on the day" runs to the day before the
-- corresponding date a month later (NOTES.md F5).  A warrant that names no officer is not
-- a warrant "authorising by name" under 22(1), so it is not valid in form either
-- (independent test pass, 2026-09-30).

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 22(1) and (6)"
GIVEN w IS A `Warrant Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the warrant is valid in form and in force when exercised` IF
        w's `the warrant names an investigation officer and one or more authorised assistants`
    AND w's `the warrant indicates the subject matter and purpose of the investigation`
    AND w's `the warrant is accompanied by a copy of the offences under sections 27, 28, 29 and 30`
    AND w's `the date on which the warrant is exercised` AT LEAST w's `the date the warrant was issued`
    AND w's `the date on which the warrant is exercised` LESS THAN `add months` (w's `the date the warrant was issued`) 1

-- 22(7) to (10): how the warrant is executed.

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 22(7), (8), (9) and (10)"
GIVEN w IS A `Warrant Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the warrant is properly executed` IF
        `the warrant is valid in form and in force when exercised` w
    AND w's `the warrant was produced to the person against whom power is exercised`
    AND (IF w's `the premises are unoccupied`
         THEN     w's `the officer took reasonable steps to inform the occupier of the intended entry`
              AND (IF w's `the occupier was informed`
                   THEN w's `the occupier or the occupier's representative was given a reasonable opportunity to be present`
                   ELSE w's `a copy of the warrant was left in a prominent place on the premises`)
              AND w's `the premises were left as effectively secured as they were found`
         ELSE TRUE)

-- 22(3) lists what the warrant authorises (entry by force, search, photographs,
-- seizure, equipment, copies, possession of documents, requiring explanations,
-- electronic information, removal of equipment); 22(5) lets equipment be retained on
-- the premises; 22(11) defines three terms.  None adds a condition: inert.

§§ `23. Post-seizure procedure`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 23(2)(a)"
GIVEN s IS A `Seizure Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the duty to provide a copy of a seized document has been met` IF
        NOT (    s's `the seized item is a document`
             AND s's `the person from whose possession the document was taken requested a copy`)
     OR s's `a copy was provided`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 23(2)(b)(i) and (ii)"
GIVEN s IS A `Seizure Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the duty to inform has been met` IF
        s's `the owner of the goods, document or information was informed of the possession, seizure or detention`
    AND (IF s's `the goods were seized from a vending machine`
         THEN s's `the proprietor named on the machine, or if none the occupier of the premises, was informed`
         ELSE TRUE)

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 23(2)(a), (b) and (c)"
GIVEN s IS A `Seizure Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the post-seizure duties have been met` IF
        `the duty to provide a copy of a seized document has been met` s
    AND `the duty to inform has been met` s
    AND s's `the goods, document or information were placed in safe custody`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 23(2)(d)"
GIVEN s IS A `Seizure Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the specified person may retain the goods, document or information` IF
        NOT s's `a court has ordered otherwise`
    AND s's `the goods, document or information retained may be evidence in those proceedings`
    AND NOT s's `proceedings under section 9 or 10 (including on appeal) are completed`

§§ `24. Power to require evidence as to identity`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 24"
GIVEN x IS AN `Examination Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the investigation officer may require evidence of identity` IF
    x's `the person is reasonably believed by an investigation officer to have engaged in an unfair practice or knowingly abetted, aided, permitted or procured a supplier to do so`

§§ `25. Power to examine, secure attendance, etc.`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 25(1)(a) and (b)"
GIVEN x IS AN `Examination Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the investigation officer may examine the person` IF
    x's `the person appears to be acquainted with facts or circumstances relevant to the investigation`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 25(1)(b) and (2)"
GIVEN x IS AN `Examination Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person must comply with the written notice to attend` IF
        x's `the person appears to be acquainted with facts or circumstances relevant to the investigation`
    AND x's `the person is within the limits of Singapore`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 25(3)(a) to (d)"
GIVEN x IS AN `Examination Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the statement complies with section 25(3)` IF
        x's `the statement is in writing`
    AND x's `the statement was read over to the person`
    AND (IF x's `the person does not understand English`
         THEN x's `the statement was interpreted in a language the person understands`
         ELSE TRUE)
    AND x's `the statement was signed by the person`

§§ `26. Self-incrimination and savings for professional legal advisers`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 26(1)"
GIVEN d IS A `Disclosure Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is not excused from disclosing on the ground that disclosure might tend to incriminate` IF
    d's `the person is required under a provision of the Act to disclose information or a document`

-- 26(2): where the person claimed before disclosing that it might incriminate,
-- the material is not admissible against the person in criminal proceedings other
-- than proceedings under Part 3B; it is admissible in civil proceedings.  The rule
-- answers whether section 26(2) bars the material's admission.

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 26(2)(a)"
GIVEN d IS A `Disclosure Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 26(2) bars admission of the material in the proceedings` IF
        d's `the person claims, before disclosing, that disclosure might tend to incriminate the person`
    AND d's `the proceedings are criminal proceedings`
    AND NOT d's `the proceedings are proceedings under Part 3B`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 26(2)(b)"
GIVEN d IS A `Disclosure Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the material is admissible in civil proceedings, including proceedings under the Act` IF
    NOT d's `the proceedings are criminal proceedings`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 26(3)(a) and (b)"
GIVEN d IS A `Disclosure Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the professional legal adviser is not compelled to disclose the privileged communication` IF
        d's `the person is a professional legal adviser, or a legal counsel in an entity, acting in that capacity`
    AND d's `the information or document is or contains a privileged communication`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 26(4)"
GIVEN d IS A `Disclosure Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the adviser must still give the name and address, if known, of the person to whom or by whom the communication was made` IF
    `the professional legal adviser is not compelled to disclose the privileged communication` d
